WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.541
There was once a swallow that lived in the green forest.

2
00:00:04.542 --> 00:00:06.279
He was handsome.

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.414
He had pretty feathers.

4
00:00:08.415 --> 00:00:13.342
The girl birds would say: "Oh, he is so handsome!

5
00:00:13.343 --> 00:00:16.759
His feathers are beautiful."

6
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.244
The swallow was proud of his good looks.

7
00:00:20.245 --> 00:00:23.990
And every day, he looked into his mirror.

8
00:00:23.991 --> 00:00:26.324
"Look at my feathers!

9
00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:29.474
They are so soft and beautiful.

10
00:00:29.475 --> 00:00:34.507
I am a lovely bird."

11
00:00:34.508 --> 00:00:37.870
One day, a crow was flying by.

12
00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:40.300
He heard the swallow singing.

13
00:00:40.301 --> 00:00:44.283
"I am so wonderful.

14
00:00:44.284 --> 00:00:47.069
I am so beautiful.

15
00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:51.998
I have the best feathers in the world."

16
00:00:51.999 --> 00:00:56.514
The crow stopped and looked at the swallow.

17
00:00:56.515 --> 00:00:59.357
"What are you singing about?"

18
00:00:59.358 --> 00:01:03.028
"I am the prettiest bird in the sky.

19
00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:05.581
You must be very jealous.

20
00:01:05.582 --> 00:01:08.186
You are not pretty like me."

21
00:01:08.187 --> 00:01:11.992
The crow became very angry.

22
00:01:11.993 --> 00:01:15.334
"Ha! You think that you are so great.

23
00:01:15.335 --> 00:01:18.742
My feathers are much better than yours."

24
00:01:18.743 --> 00:01:20.199
"You are joking!

25
00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:23.026
Your feathers are black and thick.

26
00:01:23.027 --> 00:01:27.424
Mine are light and beautiful."

27
00:01:27.425 --> 00:01:31.011
The crow and the swallow began to argue.

28
00:01:31.012 --> 00:01:34.421
They argued about who had better feathers.

29
00:01:34.422 --> 00:01:39.077
They argued and argued and argued.

30
00:01:39.078 --> 00:01:44.264
"Your feathers may be light and beautiful, but mine are much better."

31
00:01:44.265 --> 00:01:51.169
"Nonsense, only a fool would say your feathers are better than mine."

32
00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:53.077
The crow was clever.

33
00:01:53.078 --> 00:01:57.326
He could prove that his feathers were better.

34
00:01:57.327 --> 00:02:01.283
"All right! Let us go to the wise bird of the North.

35
00:02:01.284 --> 00:02:05.174
We will ask her who has better feathers."

36
00:02:05.175 --> 00:02:11.612
"I will go because I like to hear other birds tell me how wonderful my feathers look.

37
00:02:11.613 --> 00:02:15.668
The wise bird will choose me."

38
00:02:15.669 --> 00:02:21.975
So the two birds flew north to see the wise bird of the North.

39
00:02:21.976 --> 00:02:28.582
On the way to see the wise bird, the crow and the swallow passed many birds.

40
00:02:28.583 --> 00:02:34.093
All of the other birds thought that the swallow was very handsome.

41
00:02:34.094 --> 00:02:37.919
"Oh, look at him. He is handsome."

42
00:02:37.919 --> 00:02:39.616
"He sure is.

43
00:02:39.617 --> 00:02:43.597
He is the most handsome bird."

44
00:02:43.598 --> 00:02:48.075
As the birds flew north, the air became cooler.

45
00:02:48.076 --> 00:02:50.509
"I am getting cold.

46
00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:53.507
It is very cold here in the North."

47
00:02:53.508 --> 00:02:54.863
"Yes, it is.

48
00:02:54.864 --> 00:02:56.700
The North is very cold.

49
00:02:56.701 --> 00:02:59.325
We should hurry to the wise bird's house."

50
00:02:59.326 --> 00:03:02.540
"Yes, let's hurry."

51
00:03:02.541 --> 00:03:07.608
As the birds flew even further north, it started to snow.

52
00:03:07.609 --> 00:03:09.970
Now it was very cold.

53
00:03:09.971 --> 00:03:14.586
The swallow had to stop flying.

54
00:03:14.587 --> 00:03:20.061
"I am freezing. I cannot fly anymore."

55
00:03:20.061 --> 00:03:23.998
"The problem is that your feathers are not very good.

56
00:03:23.999 --> 00:03:27.028
My feathers are strong and thick.

57
00:03:27.029 --> 00:03:29.390
They keep me warm."

58
00:03:29.391 --> 00:03:33.891
The crow helped to warm the swallow with his feathers.

59
00:03:33.892 --> 00:03:37.551
"You are right! Your feathers are warm.

60
00:03:37.551 --> 00:03:39.651
They are very warm."

61
00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:42.798
"Whose feathers are better, mine or yours?"

62
00:03:42.799 --> 00:03:45.307
"I guess yours are better.

63
00:03:45.308 --> 00:03:49.388
I was too proud of my feathers."

64
00:03:49.389 --> 00:03:55.050
When the birds returned home, the swallow told everyone what had happened.

65
00:03:55.051 --> 00:03:59.922
"Crow saved my life with his wonderful feathers."

66
00:03:59.923 --> 00:04:02.571
"Hurray for Crow!"

67
00:04:02.572 --> 00:04:07.172
"Oh, Crow! You do have nice, thick, black feathers.

68
00:04:07.173 --> 00:04:10.552
They are excellent!"

69
00:04:10.553 --> 00:04:19.749
From that day on, the swallow never flaunted his feathers in front of others.

